+# ::a1 The best ice cream flavour is chocolate
+
+::a2 Every summer the same argument breaks out in our office kitchen, and every summer it ends without anyone changing their mind. ::a3 I would like to make the case properly this time. ::a4 Chocolate is the best ice cream flavour, and the reasons for it are not purely a matter of taste. ::a5 A flavour can be judged by three things, namely whether it is reliable, whether it combines well with others, and whether it survives the walk home from the shop. ::a6 Chocolate wins on all three counts, and I will take them in turn.
+
+::a7 Reliability first. ::a8 A scoop of chocolate tastes roughly the same in a cheap corner shop and in an expensive gelateria, which is emphatically not true of strawberry. ::a9 Strawberry depends entirely on the fruit, and outside of about six weeks in early summer that fruit simply is not there. ::a10 Pistachio has the opposite problem. ::a11 When it is good it is extraordinary, but most of what is sold as pistachio is dyed almond paste. ::a12 Chocolate has a floor that the other flavours do not have.
+
+::a13 The second point is about combination. ::a14 Chocolate sits next to almost anything without fighting it, which is why it ends up in every mixed cup that leaves the counter. ::a15 The third point is the most practical one. ::a16 Chocolate melts slowly and stays edible, whereas a fruit sorbet turns into coloured water within minutes. ::a17 I am aware that none of this will convince the vanilla faction, but I would at least like to hear a better argument than "vanilla goes with everything".
